d me quite gently into a vehicle and  whisked me away to the emergency room  with friends like these who needs an  ambulance after my surgery the  transition back to campus was eased by  friends who wield me between classes and  helped me navigate the lunchroom my dear  friend Christina became famous for her  willingness to kick others off the  heritage  couches so I could sit with prime leg  elevation these tells old friends didn't  pity me or just say good luck and move  along they entered into my challenge  with me they rolled up their sleeves and  said we're here to help and we managed  to have a wonderful time along the way  we laughed we cried we talked we joked  and through it all our friendships grew  and flourished as we dealt with the  struggles of that semester close friends  became best friends and college friends  became lifelong friends their kindness  inspired me and challenged me to live  more selflessly to give more readily and  to encourage more constantly in your  next four years at Hillsdale you two  will meet individuals who will share  your joys and your troubles and become  your dearest and most lasting friends  prioritize spending time with the  awesome people known as hillsdale  college students and you will not be  disappointed in addition to my friends  the Hillsdale administration and staff  helps more readily than I ever could  have expected my house mom at olds  affectionately known around campus as  mama G was only in the second day of her  job when I broke my leg yet there she  was through my whole recovery picking up  meals driving me to doctors appointments  and even welcoming me into her apartment  as a month-long roommate by the end of  that semester I found I'd been blessed  not only with a tremendous helper but  with a mentor and a friend parents mama  G is just one example of the type of  people you are leaving your children  with and I would just like to say  they're in good hands the professor's  also came through for me in my moment of  need as soon as they found out what had  happened which was pretty soon thanks to  a collegian article i received an  abundance of concerned and encouraging  emails from professors I had that  semester professors I had had previously  and professors I had never even had in  class the head of our history department  dr. Cal Toth took his lunch hour to meet  with me in the Student Union and  reorganize my schedule so that it would  be more manageable the way professors  responded reflects the way that we think  about education at Hillsdale those  professors realize that being educated  is about more than memorizing and  regurgitating a set of facts it's about  being formed as a whole person so they  care not only about our academic success  which they do care about they want to  see us grow intellectually spiritually  and personally so class of twenty  nineteen get to know them allow them to  mentor you and allow them to share their  many and abundant words of wisdom I know  office hours can be intimidating but  remember your professors truly want to  help you will all have your broken like  moments at Hillsdale you will face  challenges that make you wonder why on  earth you signed up for this it may  happen when you receive back your first  freshman paper don't worry it's rough  for all of us or as you're trying to  sort out chemical conversions in  preparation for an upcoming exam we all  have our ups and downs at Hillsdale  because this environment challenges us  to be more than we were when we arrived  but succeeding at Hillsdale isn't  something you can or should do a loan  perhaps you can squeak by without help  from others but a Hillsdale education is  about so much more than that it's about  being formed to live a good full and  flourishing life and that kind of life  must be lived in community be assured  that the type of generosity that i  received abounds at Hillsdale so  freshman class as you begin your first  year at Hillsdale immerse yourself in  this community which will show you truth  beauty and goodness where you had never  even noticed it before  and be sure to watch your step on the  ice thank you
 

